 of a particle oscillating with forced harmonic motion without damping is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+49y=-24\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the particle is initially at the origin with zero velocity, find the position of the particle after $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ seconds." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1072 #uuid "1f3b61bf-2d9c-5a4f-b827-01f0e0d4bec0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1074 "The general solution to the equation of forced harmonic motion without damping is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ represents simple harmonic motion and can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=49\\,⟹\\,\\omega =7.\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡7t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡7t.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(t).$\n\nThe external force is $-24\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,\\beta $ are constants to be determined.\n\nSubstituting ${y}_{p}$ into the differential equation and equating coefficients gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2},\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡7t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡7t-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSince the particle is initially at the origin with zero velocity, the initial conditions are $y(0)=0$ and ${y}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\nSolving with these conditions for $A$ and $B$ gives\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2},\\,B=0.\n$$\n\nSo our solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡7t-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTo find the position of the particle after $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ seconds, we substitute into the equation $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{2})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399379 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399380 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399381 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399382 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399383 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399383 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1080 #uuid "039eefc7-4800-59f4-a9af-2eb142d7c4e8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399379 1081 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399379 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399379 1084 #uuid "25213c17-424a-52a3-9371-0722697b6bae" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399380 1081 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=2\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399380 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399380 1084 #uuid "fe19165f-f1ce-59b5-81e9-0ecaae91fcfc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399381 1081 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399381 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399381 1084 #uuid "cf9a43fb-7d21-5c00-92a4-f2ea33cb0a35" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399382 1081 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\fra