0 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1071 "Consider the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ of polynomials from $R[t],$ where\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+t+{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}\\cdot {p}_{2}(t)=0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1072 #uuid "f3490611-7455-53f0-adf9-bb4a980b5cf3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1074 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ not both zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=0.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the given expressions for ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t)$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(1+t+{t}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+({x}_{2})t+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation is true for every $t$ if and only if \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the third equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=0.$ \n\nTherefore, ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly independent." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399419 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399420 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399421 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399422 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399423 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399421